Reusable operator helpers are under `.superpowers/sdd/2026-09-04-pit-optimizer-v5-campaign/` in the worktree. Run from the worktree root:

```powershell
# Use a new label for each new execution. An existing run must be inspected, not restarted.
py -3.13 -B -c "import runpy; runpy.run_path('.superpowers/sdd/2026-09-04-pit-optimizer-v5-campaign/launch-development-panel.py', run_name='__main__')" --label NEW_RUN_LABEL --policy-root .artifacts/pit-optimizer-v5/development/candidates/composite-floor-60 --sandbox-profile .artifacts/pit-optimizer-v5/evaluator/sandbox-profile-development-9b0904dca8f4.json

# Compare only after the new run has completed normally; use a new output path.
py -3.13 -B -c "import runpy; runpy.run_path('.superpowers/sdd/2026-09-04-pit-optimizer-v5-campaign/compare-development-runs.py', run_name='__main__')" --parent-run .artifacts/pit-optimizer-v5/development/runs/baseline-2021q1-02 --candidate-run .artifacts/pit-optimizer-v5/development/runs/NEW_RUN_LABEL --hypothesis .artifacts/pit-optimizer-v5/development/candidates/composite-floor-60/hypothesis.json --output .artifacts/pit-optimizer-v5/development/feedback/NEW_COMPARISON.json
```

